SOLR-2796: uniqueKey field can no longer be populated via
 <copyField/> or <field default=...>.  Also corrected CHANGES.txt entry for
 related SOLR-3495

git-svn-id: https://svn.apache.org/repos/asf/lucene/dev/trunk@1345376 13f79535-47bb-0310-9956-ffa450edef68

Here is the root cause:
The root cause of the bug is the incorrect handling of the `uniqueKey` field in the schema configuration, allowing it to be populated via `<copyField/>` or `<field default=...>`, which contradicts the intended behavior to ensure uniqueness and integrity of the unique key in SolrCloud environments. This could lead to inconsistencies in document identification and retrieval, especially in distributed setups. The changes made in the code ensure that such configurations are disallowed, enforcing stricter rules for the `uniqueKey` field.

